{"id":135354212,"slug":"yes-i-am-a-transcranial-magnetic","title":"Yes, I Am A Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation (TMS) Researcher who was in a Band Called \"The Magnets.\"","subtitle":"And now...you can hear them on Spotify ","post_date":"2023-07-22T11:40:48.576Z","audience":"everyone","type":"newsletter","canonical_url":"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/yes-i-am-a-transcranial-magnetic","wordcount":157,"source":"api","fetched_at":"2026-09-13T21:58:11.591Z","body_sha256":"e98f17112c0572763fed6a73ad10917ffd3723ff4cc95bab1c75f0c0e7bea92f","text_words":159,"complete":true,"body_html":"<p>Many of us were in promising local bands.  Few, I would imagine, have the kind of prescience to be in promising local bands that are unintentional satire as it relates to their later “life’s work.”  I write a lot about brain stimulation in psychiatry.  In college, where I chose to do no premedical studies, I was in a rock band.  The first album I personally ever recorded was also with this band.  It is now available on the internet…not because it’s amazing, but because it’s unintentionally hilarious.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lkXI!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6968cfb5-84a5-4e21-9661-0987fb89d160_1290x2197.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lkXI!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6968cfb5-84a5-4e21-9661-0987fb89d160_1290x2197.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lkXI!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6968cfb5-84a5-4e21-9661-0987fb89d160_1290x2197.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lkXI!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6968cfb5-84a5-4e21-9661-0987fb89d160_1290x2197.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lkXI!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6968cfb5-84a5-4e21-9661-0987fb89d160_1290x2197.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lkXI!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6968cfb5-84a5-4e21-9661-0987fb89d160_1290x2197.jpeg\" width=\"1290\" height=\"2197\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/6968cfb5-84a5-4e21-9661-0987fb89d160_1290x2197.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:2197,&quot;width&quot;:1290,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:1698387,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lkXI!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6968cfb5-84a5-4e21-9661-0987fb89d160_1290x2197.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lkXI!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6968cfb5-84a5-4e21-9661-0987fb89d160_1290x2197.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lkXI!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6968cfb5-84a5-4e21-9661-0987fb89d160_1290x2197.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lkXI!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6968cfb5-84a5-4e21-9661-0987fb89d160_1290x2197.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p><a href=\"https://spotify.link/DKG1lueLDBb\">Give it a listen.</a>  It includes the first song I ever wrote called, In another nod to my future in neuroscience, <em>melatonin</em>.  I am not saying it’s amazing, but I am vouching for it being funny.  (This record was before I was singing, so only one track has me on lead vocals.  If you want to hear my singing voice you will have to listen to my other music).</p><p></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p></p>","text":"Many of us were in promising local bands. Few, I would imagine, have the kind of prescience to be in promising local bands that are unintentional satire as it relates to their later “life’s work.” I write a lot about brain stimulation in psychiatry. In college, where I chose to do no premedical studies, I was in a rock band. The first album I personally ever recorded was also with this band. It is now available on the internet…not because it’s amazing, but because it’s unintentionally hilarious.\n\nGive it a listen. It includes the first song I ever wrote called, In another nod to my future in neuroscience, melatonin . I am not saying it’s amazing, but I am vouching for it being funny. (This record was before I was singing, so only one track has me on lead vocals. If you want to hear my singing voice you will have to listen to my other music).\n\nSubscribe now"}